<div style=3D'direction:ltr;margin-top:0in;margin-left:0in;width:6.5in'>
<div style=3D'direction:ltr;margin-top:0in;margin-left:0in;width:6.5in'>
<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:"Calibri Light";font-size:20.0pt' lang=
=3Den-US>Onboarding notes for new developers</p>
</div>
<div style=3D'direction:ltr;margin-top:.0423in;margin-left:0in;width:1.6416=
in'>
<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-size:10.0pt;color:#767676'><span style=3D'font-=
family:Calibri'>Tuesday, March 11, 2025</span></p>
<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-size:10.0pt;color:#767676'><span style=3D'font-=
family:Calibri'>9:30 AM</span></p>
</div>
<div style=3D'direction:ltr;margin-top:.4in;margin-left:0in;width:6.5in'>
<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Calibri;font-size:11.0pt'>Welcome to the=
 team. These notes cover the first week. Ask questions early; nobody expect=
s you to know our systems yet, and most of our setup is not obvious.</p>
<ul type=3Ddisc style=3D'direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;margin-top:0in;ma=
rgin-bottom:0in'>
<li style=3D'margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;vertical-align:middle'><span styl=
e=3D'font-family:Calibri;font-size:11.0pt'>Day 1: laptop setup, accounts, a=
nd access to Azure DevOps and the Azure portal.</span></li>
<li style=3D'margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;vertical-align:middle'><span styl=
e=3D'font-family:Calibri;font-size:11.0pt'>Day 2: clone the main repositori=
es and get the Orders API running locally.</span></li>
<li style=3D'margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;vertical-align:middle'><span styl=
e=3D'font-family:Calibri;font-size:11.0pt'>Day 3: pair with a teammate on a=
 small bug fix and go through a code review.</span></li>
<li style=3D'margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;vertical-align:middle'><span styl=
e=3D'font-family:Calibri;font-size:11.0pt'>Day 4 and 5: pick up a starter t=
icket from the board, tagged good-first-issue.</span></li>
</ul>
<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Calibri;font-size:11.0pt'>Local developm=
ent uses Docker Compose to run SQL Server and a fake payment provider. Run =
docker compose up from the repository root, then start the API from Visual =
Studio. The seed script creates ten test customers and a few hundred orders=
.</p>
<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Calibri;font-size:11.0pt'>Coding standar=
ds are in the wiki. The short version: write tests for new logic, keep pull=
 requests small, and explain the why in the pull request description rather=
 than the what, since the diff already shows the what.</p>
</div>
</div>
<br clear=3Dall style=3D'page-break-before:always'>

<div style=3D'direction:ltr;margin-top:0in;margin-left:0in;width:6.5in'>
<div style=3D'direction:ltr;margin-top:0in;margin-left:0in;width:6.5in'>
<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:"Calibri Light";font-size:20.0pt' lang=
=3Den-US>Meeting notes - API versioning discussion</p>
</div>
<div style=3D'direction:ltr;margin-top:.0423in;margin-left:0in;width:1.6416=
in'>
<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-size:10.0pt;color:#767676'><span style=3D'font-=
family:Calibri'>Thursday, April 3, 2025</span></p>
<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-size:10.0pt;color:#767676'><span style=3D'font-=
family:Calibri'>9:30 AM</span></p>
</div>
<div style=3D'direction:ltr;margin-top:.4in;margin-left:0in;width:6.5in'>
<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Calibri;font-size:11.0pt'>Attendees: Ale=
x, Priya, Sam, Jordan. Goal: agree how we version public APIs before the mo=
bile team starts using the Orders API directly.</p>
<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Calibri;font-size:11.0pt'>Options discus=
sed were URL versioning (/v1/orders), a header (api-version), and query str=
ing versioning. Priya pointed out that Azure API Management supports all th=
ree, so tooling is not the deciding factor.</p>
<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Calibri;font-size:11.0pt'>Decision: use =
URL versioning for major versions only. Minor, backwards compatible changes=
 do not get a new version. A major version stays supported for at least twe=
lve months after the next one is released.</p>
<ul type=3Ddisc style=3D'direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;margin-top:0in;ma=
rgin-bottom:0in'>
<li style=3D'margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;vertical-align:middle'><span styl=
e=3D'font-family:Calibri;font-size:11.0pt'>Action: Sam to write the version=
ing guideline page in the wiki.</span></li>
<li style=3D'margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;vertical-align:middle'><span styl=
e=3D'font-family:Calibri;font-size:11.0pt'>Action: Jordan to add /v1 routes=
 to the Orders API, keeping old routes as aliases.</span></li>
<li style=3D'margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;vertical-align:middle'><span styl=
e=3D'font-family:Calibri;font-size:11.0pt'>Action: Alex to tell the mobile =
team about the decision.</span></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<br clear=3Dall style=3D'page-break-before:always'>

<div style=3D'direction:ltr;margin-top:0in;margin-left:0in;width:6.5in'>
<div style=3D'direction:ltr;margin-top:0in;margin-left:0in;width:6.5in'>
<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:"Calibri Light";font-size:20.0pt' lang=
=3Den-US>Troubleshooting: payment webhook failures</p>
</div>
<div style=3D'direction:ltr;margin-top:.0423in;margin-left:0in;width:1.6416=
in'>
<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-size:10.0pt;color:#767676'><span style=3D'font-=
family:Calibri'>Wednesday, May 14, 2025</span></p>
<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-size:10.0pt;color:#767676'><span style=3D'font-=
family:Calibri'>9:30 AM</span></p>
</div>
<div style=3D'direction:ltr;margin-top:.4in;margin-left:0in;width:6.5in'>
<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Calibri;font-size:11.0pt'>Symptom: order=
s stay in PendingPayment even though the customer was charged. This almost =
always means the payment provider&#x27;s webhook did not reach us, or reach=
ed us and failed validation.</p>
<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Calibri;font-size:11.0pt'>First check th=
e webhook log table for the order id. If there is no row, the call never ar=
rived: check the provider dashboard for delivery errors and confirm the web=
hook URL has not changed. If there is a row with status Rejected, the signa=
ture check failed, which usually means the signing secret was rotated on on=
e side only.</p>
<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Calibri;font-size:11.0pt'>To fix a singl=
e stuck order, use the admin tool&#x27;s Reconcile button, which asks the p=
rovider for the payment status and updates the order. Do not edit the datab=
ase row by hand, because that skips the events that trigger the confirmatio=
n email.</p>
</div>
</div>
